-- Reconciliation migration. Generated by `drizzle-kit generate`, but its DDL
-- was fully redundant: every table and column it created already exists via the
-- hand-written 2026-* migrations (user_profiles, trend_items, soft-delete
-- columns, try-on and wardrobe fields, backup_logs, etc.), which are the
-- source of truth for this project's schema.
--
-- Applying the original DDL verbatim breaks fresh databases in both orders:
--   * lexical order runs this file BEFORE 2026-07-21-add-user-profiles.sql,
--     so `ALTER TABLE user_profiles ...` fails ("no such table");
--   * running it AFTER the hand-written migrations fails with duplicate
--     column errors.
--
-- This file is intentionally a no-op: it only advances the migration tracker
-- and the drizzle journal to the current schema snapshot
-- (meta/0002_snapshot.json) so future `drizzle-kit generate` runs diff
-- against the true schema instead of emitting this delta again.
SELECT 1;
